ws IOException)"}},"Files.write":{summary:"Writes bytes (or lines) to a file, creating or truncating it unless options say otherwise.",parameters:[{name:"path",meaning:"the file"},{name:"bytes",meaning:"the data"},{name:"options",meaning:"e.g. StandardOpenOption.APPEND"}],return:{meaning:"the path (throws IOException)"}},"Files.exists":{summary:"Tests whether a file or directory exists (false also when the answer cannot be determined).",parameters:[{name:"path",meaning:"the path"},{name:"options",meaning:"e.g. LinkOption.NOFOLLOW_LINKS"}],return:{meaning:"true if it exists",rules:[{when:{op:"==",value:1},meaning:"it exists"},{when:{op:"==",value:0},meaning:"not found (or not readable)"}]}},"Files.delete":{summary:"Deletes a file or an EMPTY directory (throws NoSuchFileException when missing; use deleteIfExists to ignore that).",parameters:[{name:"path",meaning:"the path"}],return:{meaning:"nothing (void)"}},"Files.createDirectories":{summary:"Creates a directory including all missing parents; no error if it already exists.",parameters:[{name:"dir",meaning:"the directory"}],return:{meaning:"the directory path"}},"Files.walk":{summary:"Lazily walks a directory tree as a Stream<Path> — close it (try-with-resources) to release directory handles.",parameters:[{name:"start",meaning:"root directory"},{name:"maxDepth",meaning:"optional depth limit"}],return:{meaning:"a Stream<Path>"}},"System.out.println":{summary:"Prints the value followed by a line separator to standard output.",parameters:[{name:"x",meaning:"any value (String.valueOf is used)"}],return:{meaning:"nothing (void)"}},"System.err.println":{summary:"Prints the value followed by a line separator to standard ERROR.",parameters:[{name:"x",meaning:"any value"}],return:{meaning:"nothing (void)"}},"System.getenv":{summary:"Reads an environment variable (or, with no argument, all of them as a Map).",parameters:[{name:"name",meaning:"variable name"}],return:{meaning:"its value, or null when it is not set",rules:[{when